  "c1-speaking-74": ["By and large, family traditions has become increasingly significant, although its implications are far from straightforward.","Not only does changing family structures raise practical concerns, but it also brings fundamental questions of responsibility to the fore.","I would argue that a more considered approach is essential, provided that it takes differing circumstances into account.","Had the potential consequences been properly anticipated, a number of decisions might well have been reconsidered.","It is important that those in positions of influence be held accountable for the outcomes of their decisions.","What is often overlooked is that established assumptions do not necessarily reflect the realities of contemporary life.","Having examined the available evidence, I would suggest that several factors are likely to shape future developments.","While the immediate advantages may be apparent, the longer-term drawbacks should not be underestimated.","The strongest counterargument is that intervention could create further complications rather than resolve the underlying issue.","Were I able to influence policy, I would prioritise sustainable measures whose effectiveness could be independently assessed."],
  "c1-speaking-75": ["Not only is family traditions a matter of immediate concern, but it also raises broader questions about the kind of society we wish to create.","What strikes me most is the extent to which changing family structures is shaped by assumptions that are rarely subjected to critical scrutiny.","Rarely can an issue of this complexity be reduced to a straightforward distinction between right and wrong.","It is widely acknowledged that meaningful progress requires more than isolated initiatives; structural change is needed.","Having taken the wider implications into account, I find it difficult to justify an approach that places short-term gains above lasting benefits.","Were it not for the competing interests involved, reaching a workable solution would undoubtedly be far less challenging.","What I find particularly compelling is the argument that responsibility ought to be shared rather than assigned to a single group.","Notwithstanding the considerable obstacles, there is reason to believe that a more equitable outcome remains achievable.","The extent to which intergenerational expectations can be addressed depends largely on whether institutions are willing to challenge established practices.","Ultimately, it is the quality of the reasoning behind a decision, rather than its immediate popularity, that ought to determine its value."],
